---
import PageShell from '../layouts/PageShell.astro'
import { PageHeader } from '../components/ui/PageHeader'
import { Tile } from '../components/ui/Tile'

const link = 'font-medium underline'
const heading = 'font-semibold'
---

<PageShell
  title="Privacy - Jingle Jam Community"
  description="What the Jingle Jam Community site collects, which analytics it uses, how long data is kept and how to change your choice."
  canonical="https://jinglejam.ostof.dev/privacy"
>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <PageHeader title="Privacy" />
    <Tile>
      <div class="flex max-w-prose flex-col gap-3 text-sm sm:text-base">
        <p class="font-semibold">Last updated: November 2026</p>
        <p>
          jinglejam.ostof.dev is a community project run by Ostof. You can get in touch at
          <a class={link} href="mailto:ostof13@gmail.com">ostof13@gmail.com</a>. The Twitch
          extension has <a class={link} href="/twitch-extension/privacy">its own privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class={heading}>Your choice</h2>
        <p>
          A banner asks whether you accept analytics. The two tools below only run if you accept,
          and declining turns both off. Your choice is kept in your browser for 12 months. You can
          change it at any time with <strong>Analytics settings</strong> at the bottom of every
          page.
        </p>

        <h2 class={heading}>Visit counter (Counterscale)</h2>
        <p>
          A self-hosted counter shows how the site is used, so it can be improved. It records the
          page, the referring site, campaign tags in the link, your
          country, and your browser and device type, including the browser's user agent. It sets no
          cookies and doesn't store your IP address. To avoid counting the same visitor twice in a
          day, it relies on your browser's cache. The data stays in the site's own Cloudflare
          account and isn't shared for any other purpose. The dashboard shows the last 90 days, and
          a longer-term copy may be kept in the same account.
        </p>

        <h2 class={heading}>Google Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Google Analytics sets cookies named <code>_ga</code> and
          <code>_ga_*</code>, configured to last about two hours, and records the pages you view,
          how you reached them and some actions, such as opening a stream or exporting a schedule.
          Advertising features are turned off. Google provides this service and may process the
          data outside the UK and EU, including in the United States. Google keeps this data for no
          longer than 14 months. If you withdraw your choice, the cookies are removed.
        </p>

        <h2 class={heading}>Logging in</h2>
        <p>
          If you log in, a <code>session</code> cookie keeps you logged in, and a
          <code>tiltify_oauth_state</code> cookie protects the login and expires after 10 minutes.
          Your account details are stored to run your profile and schedules. These are needed for
          logging in, so they aren't part of the analytics choice.
        </p>

        <h2 class={heading}>Stored in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses your browser's local storage for your theme, schedule display settings,
          dismissed banners and your analytics choice. This stays on your device.
        </p>

        <h2 class={heading}>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site runs on Cloudflare, which handles every request, including your IP address, to
          deliver and protect the site.
        </p>

        <h2 class={heading}>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask for a copy of your data, or ask to have it corrected or deleted, by emailing
          the address above. You can turn analytics off at any time with Analytics settings. In the UK you can complain to
          the <a class={link} href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's
          Office</a>, and in the EU to your national data protection authority.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Tile>
  </div>
</PageShell>
